    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes along with the full `./mvnw test` build (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that on a successful owner create, a welcome notification be enqueued by emitting a line to the logger named `NOTIFY` containing the owner id and the memberId.\n\nI implemented this in the create flow (`POST /api/owners`, handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1`):\n\n- Added a dedicated `NOTIFY` logger alongside the existing `AUDIT` logger (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:83`).\n- Added `enqueueWelcomeNotification(Owner)`, which logs `welcome notification enqueued: id={} memberId={}` with `owner.getId()` and `owner.getMemberId()`.\n- Called it in `createOwner(...)` after the owner is persisted and audited, so it only fires on a successful create.\n\nThe `memberId` used matches the value the test reads back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` (`owner.getMemberId()`), so the `NOTIFY` line contains both the owner id and memberId as required. The `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` test passes, and the full `./mvnw test` run reports **BUILD SUCCESS** (1 test, 0 failures).",
